  <content>
  <section><para>For numbers 1 – 5, select the slope and intercept that corresponds to each equation:</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="6c21e788-9cde-4e5b-94cc-e15e1e947b3f"><problem><para>
      <para>\( -4x+3y=3 \)</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para><para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para><para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para><para>\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para><para>\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para></problem><solution><para>\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<para><emphasis>Using Standard Form and Intercepts to Graph</emphasis></para>
<para> Standard form, \(Ax + By = C\), is helpful for finding the \(x\)-intercepts and \(y\)-intercepts of an equation. </para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="d693b658-f7c3-4288-9f1b-0baf9a491166"><problem><para>
      <para> For questions 6 - 11, </para>
      <blockquote>Use the equation \(6x -4y=24\).</blockquote>
      <para>What is the value of \(y\) at the \(x\)-intercept?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>0</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 0.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--BEGIN ADD DESMOS INTERATIVE-->
